<title>TUNISIA: Rate falls at Tunisian treasury auction.</title>
<headline>Rate falls at Tunisian treasury auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury raised 65 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury bills dated April 8, and repaid maturing paper totalling 17.2 million dinars.</p>
<p>Rate for two-year notes payable in equal annual tranches fell to 6.8125 percent coupon rate from 6.8750 percent last week.</p>
<p>Herewith breakdown of the auction results:</p>
<p> Maturity		    Amount   Rate   Previous week</p>
<p>-Two-year note payable in</p>
<p> equal annual tranches    25 MD   6.8125    6.8750</p>
<p>				   5 MD   6.0750	-</p>
<p>				   4 MD   6.9375	-</p>
<p>				  15 MD   7.0000	-</p>
<p>-Two-year note payable</p>
<p> at maturity		  10 MD   6.9375     6.9375</p>
<p>				   6 MD   7.0000	  -</p>
<p>Banks bid for 217 million dinars for two-year and three-year notes at between 6.8125 and 7.5 percent.</p>
<p>(one $=1.08 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
